The qualification tooling shall run pinned cargo-mutants on owned Rust sources and pinned Stryker.NET on executable managed-client behavior through discoverable real-engine contracts. These maintained frameworks shall be the primary mutation phase, receiving at most half the remaining campaign budget before library-generated property batches. Hand-selected numerical mutations shall remain separate, explicitly selected supplemental regression evidence rather than consuming the default campaign before the frameworks. Rust round-robin shard selection shall be recorded and reproducible from the campaign seed.
