[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-PROCESS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bound inherited-pipe draining and reap workspace-owned workers
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation orchestration shall apply its command cancellation budget to output draining as well as parent-process execution, retaining bounded partial diagnostics when draining cannot complete. After a tool exits, cleanup shall select only known worker executable images inside that run's unique directory; unrelated processes shall remain untouched. A regression shall exercise a child retaining inherited output after its parent exits and separately verify run-local worker cleanup.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived from the first managed replay after the soak: Stryker wrote its final report, but two orphaned run-local transport fixtures kept redirected pipes open and required identity-checked manual cleanup. Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs uses cancellation-aware reads, capped post-cancellation settling and ReapOwnedWorkers. Verification: --pipe-self-test and tests/FrameworkMutations.Tests.ps1 on Windows, plus a native Linux self-test. Cleanup is scoped best-effort process supervision, not a sandbox, arbitrary descendant containment or a hard real-time guarantee. Native compiler errors, timeouts and manual interventions remain distinct evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MUT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MAN-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Envelope guard qualification without conditional assignment rollback
STATEMENT: >>>
Managed transport shall preserve independent schema/status/completion type checks while assigning field holders independently of short-circuit validation guards. Mutation evidence shall identify native compiler failures separately and verify whether the guarded handler is compiled and tested rather than accepting a region-wide definite-assignment rollback as detection evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from Stryker CS0165/SafeMode rollback for versionValue and completion. Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Client/Client.cs initializes JSON field holders before validation. Verification: existing TransportContracts malformed-envelope cases, fresh managed coverage, and native Stryker replay reports. No compiler-error candidate is a kill; this requirement remains Draft pending broader qualification.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MAN-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MAN-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent managed error fields and useful diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
The managed transport shall reject each non-string, empty or whitespace-only native error code/message with an InvalidDataException and a nonblank diagnostic. Unsupported-version, malformed-envelope and contradictory-envelope errors shall retain nonblank diagnostics without requiring exact wording. Oversized request diagnostics shall identify the request-size limit before process startup.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from the six diagnostic/field-validation survivors in native Stryker run 20261030T124250Z-c9f5945d. Verification: TransportContracts.RejectsErrorFieldsIndependently, RejectsUnsupportedProtocolVersions, RejectsMalformedOrContradictoryEnvelopes and ClientContracts.RejectOversizedInputBeforeStartingProcess. Exact native replay evidence is retained in evidence/managed-20261030-triage.json. These finite contracts do not qualify all process/JSON failure paths.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MAN-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-CLEANUP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent cancellation-test deadline and process cleanup
STATEMENT: >>>
The cancellation regression shall bound its assertion independently of the client under test, verify that an acknowledged direct worker has exited before the client returns cancellation, require an acknowledged descendant to exit within a bounded settling interval, and independently reap both workers in test cleanup even if the client cleanup is broken. Native mutation timeouts, compiler rollbacks, conditional equivalents and unexercised operating-system behaviors shall retain separate dispositions and source identities.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: TransportContracts.CancellationStopsTheStartedChild; a copied-client cleanup-guard mutation fails the live-child assertion and the unmodified client passes. Independent cleanup prevents the test's own finally block from hiding the assertion behind an unbounded wait. WindowsWorkerHasNoConsoleWindow observes the current host only; it does not distinguish CreateNoWindow on a headless parent and is not an interactive Windows qualification claim. The Count property pattern in Client.cs avoids Stryker 5.0.0's invalid property-to-LINQ-Sum instrumentation while preserving the nonnegative Count loop condition. Replay evidence remains bounded, not formal proof.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MUT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QUAL-TRANSPORT-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded transport liveness and startup ownership qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
Every managed conformance and synthetic-fixture request shall have an independent test budget and wait limit. Production transport shall observe caller cancellation while processing synchronously completed IO/tasks. Qualification shall turn the previously hanging stdin-close, pending-removal and EOF mutations into test-reported failures before the framework timeout. The fixture shall own and reap a launched descendant if synthetic startup failure or parent-acknowledgement file failure occurs before readiness is published.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Simulator.Conformance/BoundedTestClient.cs (test-only five-second cancellation/seven-second outer wait), Client.cs cancellation checkpoints, Simulator.TransportFixture/Program.cs startup exception cleanup. Tests: StartupFailureBeforeParentAcknowledgementReapsDescendant (synthetic and actual marker collision), acknowledged cancellation theory, and the full managed suite under native Stryker 5.0.0. Stryker additional timeout is 15 seconds; this is a test failure observation allowance, not product latency or an OS containment guarantee. Evidence: evidence/five-area-transport.json and scoped coverage. Other equivalents, compiler-invalid and unexecuted platform cases remain separate; the requirement is Draft outside these finite profiles.
<<<
