[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BENCH-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Accuracy-gated external simulator comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
A paired supported-circuit comparison shall validate named OP/complex-AC/transient values with explicit coordinate units, absolute/relative bounds and declared solver/integration policies before making timing summaries eligible. It shall retain raw repetitions, excluded warmups, rotated execution order, process-inclusive elapsed time, nullable OS peak working-set measurements, available native work counters, executable/input/source hashes and versions. Missing, nonfinite, nonmonotonic or extrapolated reference data, changed inputs and expired execution budgets shall not yield eligible passing timing summaries. Build, parser and parent artifact-processing time shall be distinguished from timed child execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Benchmarks uses maintained .NET Process, Stopwatch and source-generated System.Text.Json plus the existing typed public response API; scripts/Run-ComparisonBenchmark.ps1 incrementally builds a NativeAOT helper or an explicit managed mode. Verification: Simulator.Benchmarks.Tests parser/property/process tests (FsCheck replay 372,20261031), negative CLI missing-observable timing invalidation, Pester launch bounds, and executed compat/benchmarks/suite.json pairs on ngspice and LU/faer. Evidence: evidence/five-area-benchmark.json. Small paired fixtures do not isolate solver throughput or establish full SPICE compatibility. Dynamic libraries and the OS image are not frozen; unavailable peak statistics/counters remain null. No universal performance or coverage threshold is implied.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QUAL-CONT-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Coupled nonlinear continuation with an independent oracle
STATEMENT: >>>
Bounded source and Gmin continuation shall qualify a coupled two-node antiparallel Shockley ladder under signed 30 V drive, three impedance scales and dense LU/QR and sparse faer CPU providers. Successful source continuation shall reach unit excitation. Successful Gmin continuation shall remove its shunt before accepting the physical solution. Independent nested monotone bisection, source-current and node KCL checks shall bound errors. Named positive/negative ngspice pairs shall retain exact models, temperature, numerical settings and printed-value bounds. Exhausted budgets shall remain explicit failures.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation and verification: tests/difficult_continuation.rs covers 90 matrix solves plus 32 Proptest cases (seed 2026103005) across six solver/policy combinations with 256 Newton iterations and 1e-11 A absolute current tolerance; a deliberately significant 1e-4 S final warm-start shunt makes accidental retention observable. Gmin stages list regularized solves only; final_unregularized plus physical oracle/KCL verify the separate final solve. compat/benchmarks/coupled-clamp-positive and -negative decks use 27 C, IS=1p/N=1 and IS=1f/N=1.5, zero charge/series resistance, and ngspice numerical gmin=1e-15 S. A tighter 1e-13 A/128-iteration attempt exhausted 128 source stages at scale 0.56640625; this is retained boundary evidence, not a general convergence guarantee. Evidence: evidence/five-area-continuation.json. This finite model family does not close universal convergence or arbitrary diode-model compatibility.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: INT-WORK-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Actual nonlinear initialization work accounting
STATEMENT: >>>
Configured transient work reports shall include every linear provider solve used by nonlinear operating-point initialization and adaptive coarse/half/fine attempts. Explicit initial states shall not add an initialization solve. Work counters shall describe executed work, including rejected attempts, rather than inferred step counts.
<<<
