[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QUAL-SPARSE-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Physical AC ladders and prepared transient factor qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
Direct sparse complex solves shall match independent RC continued-fraction and series-RLC impedance equations under non-unit complex excitation across bounded dimensions, scales and frequencies. Fixed BE/trapezoidal transient shall agree with the dense reference, reuse factors only for matching numeric step identities, and reject stale factors even when a provider claims the current matrix identity. Empty, nonfinite, wrong-value and explicitly failing providers and singular ideal-source loops shall fail without a hidden alternate-provider fallback. Explicit initial states shall not add an initialization solve to reported work.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/sparse_qualification.rs has direct-only provider spies whose dense entry point panics; RC counts 1..8, three impedance scales and four frequencies, plus 32 Proptest cases at seed 2026103004, and a signed series-RLC oracle. Binary step h=1/1024 s permits exact cache identities; a 1.5h PWL breakpoint requires h/2 and h factors. A lying stale-factor provider is rejected by the owning residual check. Native cargo-mutants selections and scoped compiler-mapped line coverage are retained in evidence/five-area-sparse.json. The original selected solve-counter multiplication mutant survived until an independent accepted-interval count assertion was added; its replay is killed. Finite owned-adapter evidence excludes vendor internals, prepared complex caching, GPU and production qualification. This Draft does not close the complete sparse release work package.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUD-AC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent linear complex-phasor conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Before publishing supported linear AC results, the engine shall reconstruct element currents and voltage-defined constraints directly from R/C/L, independent and controlled-source equations, not assembled matrices or another solve. It shall check every node including reference-node KCL and absorbed complex power using peak phasors S=V*conj(I)/2, explicit V/A/W/var bounds and declared source overrides. Invalid shapes, nonfinite values, invalid frequencies and duplicate/unknown/non-source overrides shall be rejected. Failed checks shall prevent a successful manifest. Nonlinear AC whose incremental bias is not retained shall report physical auditing as NotChecked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit_ac.rs, re-exported through audit.rs; src/api.rs audits raw MNA states before derived signal expansion and retains the worst discrepancy with frequency coordinates. Tests: tests/analysis_audits.rs covers RC/RLC, all controlled-source kinds, complex peak/conjugation convention, corrupted source voltage/current, extreme nominal replacement, public manifest evidence and seeded RC properties (32 cases, seed 2026103006). Evidence: evidence/five-area-audits.json and scoped coverage. Global error, nonlinear bias-dependent power and general SPICE/GPU/production qualification remain unavailable; numerical backward-error checks remain separate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUD-CONFIG-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Configured fixed-step discrete energy audit
STATEMENT: >>>
Supported configured fixed-step BE and linear trapezoidal results shall be audited independently at accepted raw MNA intervals with explicit source endpoint values. BE energy shall include its numerical dissipation; trapezoidal energy shall use midpoint voltage/current and quadratic stored-energy differences. The audit shall reconstruct capacitor displacement and signed inductor flux, current conservation and source constraints, with energy discrepancies in joules. Failed checks shall prevent publication. Adaptive accepted endpoints that omit winning half-step history shall report the physical interval audit as NotChecked rather than applying an incorrect coarse-step identity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit_configured.rs delegates nominal BE element equations after selecting source endpoint values and independently checks linear midpoint trapezoidal equations. Tests: tests/analysis_audits.rs includes sine/PWL endpoint sources, RC/RLC energy, constant-capacitance nonlinear diode BE, corrupted accepted states, invalid interval/source descriptors, seeded scales and public manifest checks. Nonlinear trapezoidal remains unsupported by the integrator and explicitly unaudited by the direct audit interface. The audit neither reads assembled matrices nor reruns numerical solvers. Evidence: evidence/five-area-audits.json. Successful physical balance does not establish global waveform accuracy; the global_accuracy check remains NotChecked.
<<<
