[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-006
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Verified checkpoint campaign admission and bounded overnight window
STATEMENT: >>>
An overnight qualification launcher shall require a clean exact source commit in the expected repository, isolate bulk outputs, preserve an existing campaign and share admission locking across linked worktrees. The actual test worker shall own the canonical repository lock throughout its campaign so termination of an outer shell does not admit overlapping tests. Requested duration and any earlier absolute finish deadline shall remain distinct in evidence. One outer dispatch anchor shall define the effective outer deadline as the earlier of requested duration expiry and optional user finish; the child shall always receive an absolute finish five seconds earlier, including duration-only runs. A remaining window of five seconds or less shall be rejected before dispatch. Tool setup, host compilation and testing shall have outer deadline supervision with monotonic/UTC reconciliation and exceptional child cleanup. Scheduled, started, incomplete, failed and completed work shall remain explicit; a late start shall not be reported as a full requested duration.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Run-VerifiedSoak.ps1, Run-Endurance.ps1 and Endurance.cs CampaignLock/CampaignBudget. Standard primary/linked .git layout; Windows launcher uses NTFS source junctions to unique E: work/target directories and reuses pinned installed tools without a production dependency. Worker records canonical lock, supervisor assembly hash, requested/effective budget and existing source/seed/mutation provenance. Outer waits reconcile external UTC at most once per second and cancel/observe losing waits; five-second test cleanup reservation stays inside the user window. Historical verification:16 Pester contracts (including actual-worker lock probes across primary/linked trees, held-lock refusal, slow bootstrap timeout and injected post-dispatch report failure), six split-clock contracts, actual Windows power acquire/release,18 Proptest methods at256 requested cases/method with seed88320261103. November3 timing follow-up:13 launcher contracts verify a common anchor for missing/later/earlier finish, too-short rejection, real six-second stuck-child cleanup and existing source/lock/report contracts; evidence/launcher-shared-deadline.json records source identities, current coverage and the earlier partial preflight. New waveform phase and analytical switch divider properties participate in changing-seed campaigns. Evidence: evidence/verified-soak-preflight.json and docs/verified-soak-window.md. Real seven-hour completion, forced-supervisor/bootstrap cleanup, forced OS suspension, separate external git-dir layouts and Linux launcher coverage remain unqualified; no Windows Job Object guarantee is claimed. Draft pending actual overnight evidence.
<<<
